#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096467 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "a30b523c-d689-520a-a708-f3b5190eaf9d" :question/math-academy-id "e-477" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{1}{1-\\sin^2 x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad  \\cos^2 x = 1-\\sin^2 x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096468 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "872b9d99-ea39-540f-af2e-acbfa28186b4" :question/math-academy-id "e-478" :question/problem "Calculate $\\, \\displaystyle{\\int} \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\tan^2{x}$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2x =\\sec^2x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x =\\sec^2 x -1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\left(\\sec^2 x -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\tan x -x+C.\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096469 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "d7c09fca-2f4b-5a0a-b687-938527b44d62" :question/math-academy-id "e-479" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+\\cot^2x =\\csc^2 x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\cot^2 x &=\\csc^2 x -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\bigg(5\\left(\\csc^2 x -1 \\right) -x^2\\bigg) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\int \\left(5\\csc^2 x -5 -x^2\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=-5\\cot x -5x-\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096470 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/id #uuid "14ab2251-66fc-5f94-9821-f14fcc2c03e1" :question/math-academy-id "e-480" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d} x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity  $1+\\tan^2 \\theta =\\sec^2 \\theta$ with $\\theta = 3x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t1+\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x)\\\n\t\t\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x) -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x&= 2\\int \\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                &= 2\\int \\left(\\sec^2 (3x) -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                 &= 2\\left(\\int \\sec^2 (3x)\\, \\textrm{d}x -\\int1 \\, \\textrm{d}x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t                                &= 2\\left( \\dfrac{1}{3}\\tan (3x) -x\\right)+C\\\n                                                                 &= \t\\dfrac{2}{3}\\tan (3x) -2x+C.\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03b7b03d-566b-57ff-9b57-89245c891150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247450} {:answer/id #uuid "258d518c-1393-51c3-9f47-dac610e236f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247755} {:answer/id #uuid "6da8f4fb-e78a-5608-aaf9-5f82ea791cb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248397} {:answer/id #uuid "6e400284-d57a-58fe-928b-40d3a6d7f47d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248400} {:answer/id #uuid "772c83ac-213f-55d7-9be6-27ef7871587f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "772c83ac-213f-55d7-9be6-27ef7871587f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248473} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e185e9d-354f-5cb8-8cd3-194e9a76c8b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47d60902-14e4-57db-9a3c-83c4f5318199" :question/math-academy-id "q-114435" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =0-0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d22de40-ea9d-5b02-b173-001334c7aa47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436406} {:answer/id #uuid "a179ef6b-2edf-5a1b-a42e-681c262094e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436416} {:answer/id #uuid "a9eea812-8b18-5d6c-8b4a-96c0c0fdf7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436418} {:answer/id #uuid "c036b8c0-7240-5495-8524-f123ce10d9ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436420} {:answer/id #uuid "e4e1cdb2-01c4-599a-b0e1-dac97bfc07ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡1-\\operatorname{csc}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d22de40-ea9d-5b02-b173-001334c7aa47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436406} :answer-field/id #uuid "05543962-4127-57e7-802c-654a5d1cc094" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "67ca50b0-637c-5544-b80a-0086acfa0a59" :question/math-academy-id "q-114468" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{1}^{2}(2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-1)-3+2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-1))\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity ${sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ with $\\theta =\\frac{x}{3}-1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-1)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-1)-3+2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-1))\\text{d}x & = \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{2}(2[{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-1)]-3)\\text{d}x & = \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{2}(2(1)-3)\\text{d}x & = \\\\ -{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\text{d}x & = \\\\ -x\\,{|}_{1}^{2} & = \\\\ -(2-1) & = \\\\ -1 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250274 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "429c4e06-3048-55b1-b208-72019f1b0474" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248017} {:answer/id #uuid "7e54eb59-7b2b-5295-a85f-69bab12eefd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248535} {:answer/id #uuid "8021e056-c15c-5db2-b077-c41b6d899f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248549} {:answer/id #uuid "848e9fc1-831c-51f0-9f79-1b100b19ee3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248600} {:answer/id #uuid "b94c2031-9662-5675-9f0a-6203b77aab15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e54eb59-7b2b-5295-a85f-69bab12eefd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248535} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0cd4974-971c-56d8-b46a-a70cd95372ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a520c33d-1aa5-5864-8fa9-daf66894b11e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114469" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ with $\\theta =2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})={sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{[{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+1]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C & .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3664de6-d101-5f3f-b8ae-800b29d566b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3664de6-d101-5f3f-b8ae-800b29d566b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318126} :answer-field/id #uuid "169f7f1d-db26-55ad-9330-bc1460e5358d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb1a86d3-f725-5234-baee-3e7bfe9e8077" :question/math-academy-id "q-346553" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =0-0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f938ab7-2fee-5212-a3d5-1a636aa8f01c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f938ab7-2fee-5212-a3d5-1a636aa8f01c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436403} :answer-field/id #uuid "47b0b5ff-9531-59e7-8cea-348236536a5c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "395c9bcf-c73e-5ebd-b5f5-5752cb5f3e44" :question/math-academy-id "q-352622" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{4}-1}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x+x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{4}-1}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x+x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{4}-1}\\frac{1}{1+x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)\\,{|}_{0}^{{e}^{4}-1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡[1+({e}^{4}-1)]-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+0) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{4})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =4-0 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436441 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e17c38ec-6906-5229-841a-2efe64cdf94b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e17c38ec-6906-5229-841a-2efe64cdf94b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436421} :answer-field/id #uuid "d26c1e60-1d16-502f-81c1-ec7f13cd31c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "601c3d78-5b89-5552-acb7-b5618e1d28f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-352629" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{2{sin}^{3}⁡x}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{2{sin}^{3}⁡x}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})] \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436438 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18079da6-58a4-549e-98f0-7b53cc7a9c72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18079da6-58a4-549e-98f0-7b53cc7a9c72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436399} :answer-field/id #uuid "e099fb0b-5d08-54ae-a545-4841ad9b09ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4611fa95-3984-5432-82fc-4aa1ab6a6967" :question/math-academy-id "q-352630" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡x+x+2{cos}^{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡x+x+2{cos}^{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+2({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+2\\cdot 1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{x+2}\\,{|}_{2}^{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{7+2}-\\sqrt{2+2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{9}-\\sqrt{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436443 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87f28fc4-335f-515f-b4a3-dc2afe725bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87f28fc4-335f-515f-b4a3-dc2afe725bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436411} :answer-field/id #uuid "de843182-7831-5a84-81e5-3228bf7e7dcc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7bc6f22d-8d3d-514a-8037-cf0e1ab0434e" :question/math-academy-id "q-352651" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}x(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x){cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.$ Substituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}x(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x){cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}x{sec}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64dedadd-0d5b-56a4-a48b-8d951ecd5865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-2\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64dedadd-0d5b-56a4-a48b-8d951ecd5865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-2\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319700} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e4fc3ea-da9e-59c7-a0e0-47d8251661de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5f1d4130-f1fa-520f-a18a-606ae77d72dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-352709" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\pi /2}({cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{2}⁡x=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\pi /2}({cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi /2}(2x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-x)\\,{|}_{1}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =({(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-({1}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-2\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bcde715-09f6-55d0-9e0a-cb7faecc72f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bcde715-09f6-55d0-9e0a-cb7faecc72f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319859} :answer-field/id #uuid "d949c466-9f8a-51dc-9620-89072bd789f0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c03309dc-5937-5269-a513-e248a0216700" :question/math-academy-id "q-352747" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}[4{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+3{x}^{2}+4{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)]\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the identity ${sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ with $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2}-1,$ we get \n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[4{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+3{x}^{2}+4{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)]\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[3{x}^{2}+4({sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1))]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{x}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}+4x]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[{1}^{3}+4(1)]-[{0}^{3}+4(0)] \\\\  & =5-0 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323773 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fa96cf1-4d31-5deb-b3f4-3a3294848a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fa96cf1-4d31-5deb-b3f4-3a3294848a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321270} :answer-field/id #uuid "17fe46a9-616b-5b04-b80d-53e10861f0fe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39b5bd8a-dd36-5527-89de-e36f567f0906" :question/math-academy-id "q-362509" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{1-{tan}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwe compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{1-{tan}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89a639e1-ea30-5852-945d-838c01f3a530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322245} {:answer/id #uuid "80e254bb-01fa-560a-b35d-95dbd95c9a3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80e254bb-01fa-560a-b35d-95dbd95c9a3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436409} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfbc300f-8435-5b63-80a7-df2fbc495791" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a3e4c61-3446-503d-9221-974875074079" :question/math-academy-id "q-362530" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =0-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "276aab9b-ffdf-5b59-bf38-04c9aff0899f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "276aab9b-ffdf-5b59-bf38-04c9aff0899f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436401} :answer-field/id #uuid "a395c87e-abf9-5742-944f-23bde4fbd8e1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436430}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "abe2124c-7cb3-538b-9274-4eab950d2782" :question/math-academy-id "q-362798" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({tan}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So, we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({tan}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x({tan}^{2}⁡x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}-(-2) \\\\  & =2-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7841411-b2a3-5f14-a4fa-569475a21ff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7841411-b2a3-5f14-a4fa-569475a21ff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323091} :answer-field/id #uuid "274f1f5a-362f-555e-b4c6-9b261c2ad7ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "053d1129-5ad9-5392-8059-7eab09c97e80" :question/math-academy-id "q-362804" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{csc}^{4}⁡x-1}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{csc}^{4}⁡x-1}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)({csc}^{2}⁡x+1)}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436439 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b4fbc1c-3545-5745-89f4-848a4e77fc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436398} {:answer/id #uuid "6779cc08-804c-549e-a688-72a8c218ac7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436405} {:answer/id #uuid "70b508c8-5bef-5ba4-be2d-d5c002a6fd14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436407} {:answer/id #uuid "949785f1-bc84-54a6-aa50-79802f8ac400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436414} {:answer/id #uuid "b96b832a-78b1-56de-b64f-6e8bbc3e0065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b96b832a-78b1-56de-b64f-6e8bbc3e0065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436419} :answer-field/id #uuid "fde1e6aa-3904-5bc7-8bc1-4efe5c7c9097" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a652b8e-bfd2-5735-84e4-910c649c4ba7" :question/math-academy-id "q-49323" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity  ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ with $\\theta =x+\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+{sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =1 \\\\ {sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-1 & =-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "008298da-bf7a-51ca-837d-ab329d0489ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329955} {:answer/id #uuid "099d6ddf-d5f2-5fd1-9989-6721d1ea7bce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330034} {:answer/id #uuid "88ac8b32-2829-5bde-aed3-69f279dfedfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331164} {:answer/id #uuid "97b2c286-d293-598e-8173-52cb4aaa72e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331301} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c3c459-f04c-5677-8215-e3b74b9824f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2c3c459-f04c-5677-8215-e3b74b9824f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331681} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2910a34-30ac-5541-b445-de1db206308c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d70cb193-c0f3-511e-a986-3ca7b8cef3f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-49332" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{1-{cot}^{4}⁡x}{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  \n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{1-{cot}^{4}⁡x}{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0860c1d8-216d-5466-9f62-ccae7b52e912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330020} {:answer/id #uuid "203a6ea8-eba0-5d40-aa09-a59a360ffbdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330226} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb98399-a9d4-5fe9-bc96-644e80f830a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330488} {:answer/id #uuid "823db0e7-2377-5017-b419-f145d5d9961d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331099} {:answer/id #uuid "8a3e9f10-f5ea-57a0-9d29-03b20270bd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a3e9f10-f5ea-57a0-9d29-03b20270bd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331177} :answer-field/id #uuid "a10a89c1-f082-55be-bb60-453abc8e5020" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "71ebda71-dbd6-53ac-9e9c-22ae8c3a8413" :question/math-academy-id "q-49446" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.$ \nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}=\\frac{1}{-{sin}^{2}⁡x}=-{csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436436 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0697a92c-8206-5e12-8a38-d0cce8f0b796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+5{cot}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436396} {:answer/id #uuid "0ad53142-ca5c-5050-8255-c2bf7f34c973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-5\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436397} {:answer/id #uuid "2396ae55-dd62-5c4f-8d14-716f3b077ffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-5{cot}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436400} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0f1722-492f-5d0d-b85d-b801f734974d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436408} {:answer/id #uuid "f7191b76-8b73-524d-9752-f1a9544d8d3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ad53142-ca5c-5050-8255-c2bf7f34c973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-5\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436397} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e7afbe3-da6c-5c70-9675-1af28ae108a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ab531ef-b57e-5769-8250-354ac0b4cc1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-73517" :question/problem "$\\int ({x}^{2}+5{cot}^{2}⁡x+5)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Substituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}+5{cot}^{2}⁡x+5)\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}+5({cot}^{2}⁡x+1))\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({x}^{2}+5{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-5\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03bdaab2-0459-58ae-a8b6-8b7e961433b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436395} {:answer/id #uuid "4473c0b8-d717-5666-b3a5-b13736dbd9a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436402} {:answer/id #uuid "543e21b0-8a43-5f83-99a5-6a65c94df81a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436404} {:answer/id #uuid "82bb6b98-f551-51d7-8c45-510ea2939429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436410} {:answer/id #uuid "916d355a-d995-57ca-985a-adb9f65e34b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "916d355a-d995-57ca-985a-adb9f65e34b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436413} :answer-field/id #uuid "a76e6cf8-d6fc-5fed-b981-732822fa34e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cfd5d01f-68da-5044-a541-b2046cbc9096" :question/math-academy-id "q-73527" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (8{x}^{3}-2{tan}^{2}⁡x-2)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x+1={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (8{x}^{3}-2{tan}^{2}⁡x-2)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (8{x}^{3}-2({tan}^{2}⁡x+1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (8{x}^{3}-2{sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b659d5b-ffc1-56c2-ab05-c2b4ce6bb943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436412} {:answer/id #uuid "97915e10-8926-58fa-8c08-872ae939879a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436415} {:answer/id #uuid "a52f2e45-3e7d-50ca-b3ac-e9182e500551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436417} {:answer/id #uuid "e73f1488-a01d-5db0-b321-5aa7c70413f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436423} {:answer/id #uuid "f7449390-3d4e-54f0-a121-f8acf6006130" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7449390-3d4e-54f0-a121-f8acf6006130" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436425} :answer-field/id #uuid "18c90a23-59a9-5282-89e5-a5dfddf8ce79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436427}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5e890818-44b2-5fa4-a0b6-4c9a2cfbfd6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73529" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(1-{cot}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =x-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & ={csc}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ {cot}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & ={csc}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(1-{cot}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(1-{csc}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(2-{csc}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}2\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}{csc}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =2(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+0-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
